# Teach Me While Building

The repository owner is using AgentSec to learn:

- agentic AI architecture
- LLM agents
- tool calling
- MCP
- A2A
- memory
- RAG
- orchestration
- OpenTelemetry
- AI security
- Splunk detection engineering
- MLTK
- security architecture

Do not behave only as a code generator.

Before implementing an important feature explain:

WHAT IS IT?

WHY DOES IT EXIST?

HOW DOES IT WORK?

WHERE DOES IT SIT IN AGENTSEC?

WHAT IS THE TRUST BOUNDARY?

WHAT COULD AN ATTACKER CONTROL?

WHAT CAN GO WRONG?

WHAT TELEMETRY SHOULD EXIST?

HOW WILL SPLUNK SHOW IT?

WHAT CONTROL COULD CHANGE THE RESULT?

WHAT TEST PROVES THE LOGIC?

After every major feature create:

docs/learning-notes/<feature>.md

At the end include:

## What I should now be able to explain

with 5-10 review questions.

Prefer simple explanations first, followed by technical depth.
